                <person xml:id="DEN01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Jonathan /Robert</forename>
                        <surname>Dennet</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000-01-01">
                        <placeName/>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000-12-31"/>
                    <occupation>Attorney</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>See Ed Pope's note: Jonathan and Robert Dennett with William Greaves and
                            Henry Townley Ward, attorneys 2 Henrietta-st Covent Garden from 1789 or
                            earlier. Jonathan Dennett of Lincolns Inn will PCC 21.4.1818 formerly of
                            Leicester-place Soho mentioned sister Margaret, house in Croston, Lancs,
                            wife Eliza, children Harriet and Frances Eliza dated 7.10.1806 codicil
                            5.1.1814 wife dead, bro Robert codicil 14.2.1816 dau Harriet married to
                            Richard Richards. Jonathan Dennett of Covent garden = Liverpool
                            29.12.1786 Eliza Greaves. He died 12.4.1818, Robert D died 14.5.1837 and
                            he and Wm Greaves dissolved a partnership with M Tatham 3.10.1825.
                            Jonathan D voted Hood and Fox 1784, Fox 1796, Robert D voted Hood 1788 The
                            Tatham (probabbly Meaburn Tatham) in 1816 tends to clinch this identity
                        </p>
                    </note>
